<section data-screen-label="Grease Trap Cleaning Hero" style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;height:380px;display:flex;align-items:center;background:#716558;color:#fff;padding:0 20px">
  <div style="position:absolute;inset:-20px;background:url('https://i0.wp.com/jbgplumbingtx.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/Grease-trap-cleaning.jpg') center/cover no-repeat;filter:blur(7px)"></div>
  <div style="position:absolute;inset:0;background:rgba(113,101,88,.8)"></div>
  <div style="position:relative;width:100%;max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto">
    <h1 style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(44px,7vw,96px);line-height:1;font-weight:900;color:#fff">Grease Trap Cleaning</h1>
    <div style="width:60px;height:4px;background:#BD1E2D;margin-top:20px"></div>
    <p style="margin:20px 0 0;max-width:720px;font-size:clamp(18px,1.8vw,22px);line-height:1.5;color:#fff">Clean Grease Trap Lines</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="background:#fff;padding:clamp(56px,7vw,100px) 20px"><div style="max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="margin:0 0 20px;text-align:center;font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,52px);line-height:1.1;font-weight:800;color:#2B2622">Clean Grease Trap Lines</h2><div style="width:60px;height:4px;background:#BD1E2D;margin:0 auto 28px"></div><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,440px),1fr));gap:clamp(20px,4vw,56px)"><p style="margin:0;font-size:19px;line-height:1.7;color:#2B2622">Your grease trap is an integral part of your restaurant or food business – so don't wait until it starts causing you problems. Grease traps must be cleaned on a regular basis. Not only that, but the drain lines should also be cleaned and flushed to keep them flowing free. Failing to clean your grease traps can result in serious problems. These problems start when grease builds up and stops the flow through the trap.</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:19px;line-height:1.7;color:#2B2622">Such a situation is a major hassle – not to mention it's messy. It can shut an otherwise smooth operating business down in the blink of an eye. So, make sure to schedule repair visits from a professional plumber to clean your grease trap lines and the rest of your grease trap.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="background:#F4F1EE;padding:clamp(56px,7vw,100px) 20px"><div style="max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="margin:0 0 20px;text-align:center;font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,52px);line-height:1.1;font-weight:800;color:#2B2622">Commercial Grease Traps</h2><div style="width:60px;height:4px;background:#BD1E2D;margin:0 auto 28px"></div><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto"><p style="margin:0;font-size:19px;line-height:1.7;color:#2B2622">Most food establishments, including restaurants, are required by local laws to have a grease trap in their commercial kitchen. The goal of the grease trap is to capture grease as well as fat and oil. The popular acronym FOG (fat, oil, grease) is an easy way to remember what grease traps capture. Grease traps slow the draining of water so that these substances are allowed to congeal. The congealing makes them too large to pass through the grease trap into the rest of the drainage system. Grease traps prevent fat, oil, and grease from entering your restaurant's plumbing. If they do, they can cause serious problems and expensive repairs. Even more important, they prevent these substances from entering the city water system. Not only will you be fined if more than the minimum amount of FOG enters the city water system from your food business, but the situation can quickly spiral out of control. An overflowing grease trap into the community sewer lines can cause blockages. This will result in water backing up into homes, businesses, and even streets connected to that sewer line. Avoid this problem by having your commercial grease traps cleaned and inspected on a regular basis.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="background:#fff;padding:clamp(56px,7vw,100px) 20px"><div style="max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="margin:0 0 20px;text-align:center;font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,52px);line-height:1.1;font-weight:800;color:#2B2622">Why Grease Trap Lines Must Be Cleaned</h2><div style="width:60px;height:4px;background:#BD1E2D;margin:0 auto 28px"></div><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto"><p style="margin:0 0 32px;text-align:center;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,30px);line-height:1.4;font-weight:800;color:#716558;padding:20px 0;border-top:2px solid #E6E0DA;border-bottom:2px solid #E6E0DA">The short and sweet answer is: to prevent clogs and damages.</p><p style="margin:0;font-size:19px;line-height:1.7;color:#2B2622">Cleaning a grease trap by yourself is difficult. Not only that, but it's dirty and time consuming without the proper tools and equipment. That's where our professionals enter the picture. Our trained plumbers know exactly how to clean grease traps in a timely and effective manner. The end product is a grease trap that works well. It won't back up and cause serious problems for your restaurant. It will ensure that you don't get fined by the local government. In addition to cleaning grease traps, we also clean the grease trap lines and inspect the rest of your plumbing. Such regular plumbing inspections are an essential part of capturing problems in their infancy before they develop into full-fledged problems.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="background:#F4F1EE;padding:clamp(56px,7vw,100px) 20px"><div style="max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto"><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:var(--gtCols);gap:24px;align-items:stretch"><div style="background:#fff;border-radius:6px;border-top:4px solid #BD1E2D;box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(43,38,34,.12);padding:clamp(22px,2.4vw,32px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0;font-weight:900;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.01em;font-size:22px;line-height:1.2;color:#2B2622">Grease Trap Cleaning Service</h3><p style="margin:0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:#3A3530">We know grease traps. Sure, a normal plumber might be able to do the job, but do they have specific experience with grease traps? When it comes to commercial grease trap lines, our plumbers know what to do. They have extensive experience working on commercial plumbing and grease traps, so that they provide the absolute best service and repairs. We also offer a wide variety of related services including inspection, maintenance, repair, and installation.</p></div><div style="background:#fff;border-radius:6px;border-top:4px solid #BD1E2D;box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(43,38,34,.12);padding:clamp(22px,2.4vw,32px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0;font-weight:900;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.01em;font-size:22px;line-height:1.2;color:#2B2622">Grease Trap Inspection and Maintenance</h3><p style="margin:0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:#3A3530">Clean grease trap lines equal a healthy grease trap system. But you should also have them inspected regularly in addition to cleaned. Inspection catches any problems in the bud before they develop. Regular inspection is also the key to regular maintenance. We can identify which problems need work and then fix them before they turn into costly repairs. Grease trap inspection and maintenance is a key part of a healthy grease trap system.</p></div><div style="background:#fff;border-radius:6px;border-top:4px solid #BD1E2D;box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(43,38,34,.12);padding:clamp(22px,2.4vw,32px);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;min-width:0"><h3 style="margin:0;font-weight:900;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.01em;font-size:22px;line-height:1.2;color:#2B2622">Grease Trap Repair and Installation</h3><p style="margin:0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:#3A3530">Problems do happen. There's no getting around that. If a component of your grease trap breaks, we're here to repair it. We'll send our team in to assess the nature of the problem and complete the necessary repairs. We also provide installation. If a new grease trap is deemed necessary, we will replace the old ones along with the grease trap lines. Installation is also available to new commercial kitchens. We can install the best grease trap so your business takes off on the right foot. Not only do we handle the install itself, but we also ensure that the system you get is the right one. We obtain the necessary permits before installing it for you.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section style="background:#fff;padding:clamp(56px,7vw,100px) 20px"><div style="max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="margin:0 0 20px;text-align:center;font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,52px);line-height:1.1;font-weight:800;color:#2B2622">How Clean Grease Trap Lines Help</h2><div style="width:60px;height:4px;background:#BD1E2D;margin:0 auto 28px"></div><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto"><p style="margin:0;font-size:19px;line-height:1.7;color:#2B2622">The job of a grease trap is inherently a dirty one. They receive uncalculatable amounts of fat, oil, and grease on a daily basis. Of course, problems will arise if maintenance and cleaning isn't used. The best way to maintain the life of your grease trap system is regular cleaning. Have them cleaned on a regular basis to prevent backups and costly repairs. A service like ours keeps an eye out while cleaning your grease traps for any repairs or maintenance that needs to be completed. This way we're performing an inspection on your grease trap during the cleaning process. Simply put, cleaning your grease trap lines on a regular basis will keep the system working well for years into the future.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="background:#2B2622;padding:clamp(56px,7vw,100px) 20px"><div style="max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="margin:0 0 20px;text-align:center;font-size:clamp(30px,4vw,52px);line-height:1.1;font-weight:800;color:#fff">Take Action Now</h2><div style="width:60px;height:4px;background:#BD1E2D;margin:0 auto 28px"></div><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto"><p style="margin:0;font-size:19px;line-height:1.7;color:#E6E0DA">Don't wait – your grease trap is imperative to your food establishment. Put off clean grease trap lines and you might experience a serious problem in the middle of a busy day – or even a busy rush. There's usually no getting around such a disaster when it happens. Your restaurant will have to shut down until cleaning or repairs can be made. So, check with us for a regular grease trap cleaning schedule. We normally recommend they be cleaned about every month, but it depends on the specific model. Protect your grease traps with our cleaning and maintenance services.</p></div></div></section>
